{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 38,
  "title": "The months",
  "description": "Name the months, and say when something happens.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "The months are the one set of nouns in Spanish that never takes an article, and there are twelve of them, so this unit does the first ten.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The months",
        "body": "Enero, febrero, marzo, abril, mayo, junio, julio, agosto, septiembre and octubre. All of them are masculine, but you never use the article with them: en mayo, en octubre. When you give the day as well, the day comes first and de follows: el 5 de mayo.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "en enero",
            "en": "in January"
          },
          {
            "es": "el 5 de mayo",
            "en": "the fifth of May"
          },
          {
            "es": "en agosto",
            "en": "in August"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The two short ones",
        "body": "Mayo and junio are the short months, and the -o of mayo drops when you add something to it: el primero de mayo, the first of May. The others keep their -o: el 3 de marzo, el 12 de octubre.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el primero de mayo",
            "en": "the first of May"
          },
          {
            "es": "el 3 de marzo",
            "en": "the third of March"
          },
          {
            "es": "el 12 de octubre",
            "en": "the twelfth of October"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
